    <http://example.org/node/chunk105> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To comply with The client regulatory requirements, we can implement the following security measures based on we company context:  we are already certified with ISO 27001 since 2023, which covers the development, delivery, and operations of we services. certified includes data protection measures such as encryption in transit using TLS 1.3 and encryption at rest using AES-256. we key management is handled through the EU-based infrastructure." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk106> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For hosting data within the EU and not transferring data outside, we partner with OuraneCloud, which holds the SecNumCloud qualification at the hosting layer. partner supports sovereign hosting of confidential data within the EU, addressing The client requirements for data sovereignty." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk107> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To protect sensitive data, we can leverage we existing measures such as strict partitioning with logical isolation per client and per mission, access controls to prevent any cross-client circulation of data, pseudonymisation, and data minimisation. we also have configurable retention aligned to legal archival obligations." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk108> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For audit and compliance purposes, we maintain a data processing register, have a DPO appointed, and we Data Protection Agreement (DPA) is aligned with GDPR Article 28. we log every access and system output for auditing purposes, ensuring completeness of the audit trail. we solution, Atelier, is designed to provide explainability and auditability, including features like grounded sources, retrieval trace, and figure source linking. designed aligns with the requirement to ground figures or factual statements in source documents and to provide explainability of solution outputs." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk109> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Regarding validation and signing of deliverables, while we have measures for secure development and delivery, the actual validation and signing by a chartered accountant or statutory auditor would need to be ensured through contractual agreements or service level agreements (SLAs) that respect auditor independence and separation of duties." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk11> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Assistance in drafting client letters and correspondence, mission notes, file memos and syntheses." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk110> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Finally, respecting anti-money laundering obligations is crucial. we are familiar with the anti-money laundering framework (LCB-FT) and the requirement not to undermine a firm's reporting obligations, which will guide we implementation to ensure compliance with these requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk111> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By implementing and adhering to these measures, we can satisfy The client regulatory requirements regarding GDPR compliance, data hosting, protection of sensitive data, audit trail completeness, explainability, validation of deliverables, respect for auditor independence, separation of duties, and anti-money laundering obligations." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk112> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client requires respecting professional secrecy and confidentiality, ensuring strict respect of professional secrecy, confidentiality of client data, strict partitioning of client files, protecting sensitive data, complying with GDPR, hosting data within the EU, not transferring data outside the EU, protecting sensitive data with encryption pseudonymisation, grounding figures or factual statements in source documents, providing completeness of audit trail, explaining solution outputs, validating and signing deliverables, respecting auditor s independence, separation of duties, anti money laundering obligations, legal retention and archival obligations for accounting documents." ;
